    "question": {
      ":question/id": "96f52331-9085-52ca-a0e0-d88a3410cab6",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{33}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-3C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-4C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-3C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2}-4C_{3}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
