      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{21}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+4C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 7 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}+C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+4C_{1}$.",
