      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & -12 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{11}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-6C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & -12 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}-6C_{1}$.",
