      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of $a_{21}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-9C_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}-9C_{1}$.",
