      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -7 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -11 & -7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{3}$ and $C_{2}:=C_{2}-C_{3}$.",
